      "math_academy_id": "q-78599",
      "sequence_position": 4,
      "problem": "Which of the following integers belong to the residue class $[9]_{13}?$\n\nI. $4$\n\nII. $-17$\n\nIII. $35$",
      "worked_solution": "The residue class $[9]_{13}$ consists of the elements that are congruent to $9$ modulo $13.$ So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[9]_{13} & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x≡9\\,(\\text{mod}\\,13)\\} \\\\  & =\\{x\\in Z\\,|\\,x=9+13k,\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{9+13k\\,|\\,k\\in Z\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,\\,9-2\\cdot 13,\\,9-13,\\,9,\\,9+13,\\,9+2\\cdot 13,\\,…\\} \\\\  & =\\{…,-17,-4,9,22,35,…\\}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $-17$ and $35$ belong to $[9]_{13},$ while $4$ does not.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\".",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
